course: dictionary
lesson: 7832
title: Who is a rabbi?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rabbi is a Jewish religious leader and teacher who leads a community. You can find clues in the sentence «The synagogue is the Jewish place of prayer and study, and a rabbi is a teacher and leader.» It tells you two jobs at once: teacher and leader.
explain: Read the words around rabbi for more clues. A rabbi explains the holy books, leads services in a synagogue and helps at big family events. Ask yourself: what kind of person would fit here? A rabbi fits where a leader and teacher is needed.
explain: The phrases «the rabbi of the synagogue» and «ask the rabbi» show that people go to a rabbi for help and guidance. When you are not sure of a word, check the context, then use a dictionary to confirm.
fact: A rabbi is a Jewish religious leader and teacher.
fact: A rabbi explains the Torah, the Jewish holy books.
fact: A rabbi leads services in a synagogue, the Jewish place of prayer and study.
fact: Rabbis help at weddings, bar and bat mitzvahs and funerals.
fact: Many rabbis visit schools to explain Jewish festivals such as «Passover» and «Hanukkah».
exercise: «The synagogue is the Jewish place of prayer and study, and a rabbi is a teacher and leader.» What is a rabbi? | *A Jewish religious leader and teacher | A loud musical instrument | A type of Jewish holy book | A shop that sells bread
exercise: Which of these is a job a rabbi often does? | Sells fish at the market | *Leads prayers in a synagogue | Drives a bus to school | Mends roads
exercise: Find and copy one word from «The synagogue is the Jewish place of prayer and study» that names a place. | Jewish | *synagogue | prayer | study
test: Which holy book does a rabbi explain? | *The Torah | A cookbook | The Times | A map of the world
test: «Many rabbis visit schools to explain Jewish festivals.» Which festival is named in the lessons? | Diwali | *Hanukkah | Easter | Christmas
exam: Based on the lessons, which best describes a rabbi? | A maths teacher who never goes to services | *A Jewish religious leader and teacher who leads a community | A cook who makes bread for the synagogue | A person who only works at weddings
